## TIME COMPLEXITY

FFT uses Divide and Conquer.

At each level, the array is divided into 2 parts:

T(n) = 2T(n/2) + O(n)

Here:

2T(n/2) → two recursive FFT calls
O(n)    → combine step



Using Master Theorem:

T(n) = O(n log n)
FFT(A)              = O(n log n)

FFT(B)              = O(n log n)

Point-wise multiply = O(n)

Inverse FFT         = O(n log n)

Total:

O(n log n) + O(n log n) + O(n) + O(n log n)

= O(n log n)



Time Complexity = O(n log n)
Space Complexity = O(n)
